---
import GuidePage from '../../components/GuidePage.astro';
---

<GuidePage
  title="How Much Extra Quilt Backing Do You Need?"
  guideSlug="how-much-extra-backing"
  guideCategory="reference"
  description="Add backing overage on every side, then account for panel joins, usable fabric width, direction, and your longarmer's requirements."
>
  <section>
    <h2>Add overage to all four sides</h2><p>
      An editable 4-inch-per-side default adds 8 inches to both quilt
      dimensions. A 60 × 72 inch top therefore starts with a 68 × 80 inch
      backing rectangle.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Confirm the real requirement</h2><p>
      Four inches is a conservative longarm-oriented convenience, not a
      universal rule. Measure the completed top and follow your quilter's frame,
      clamp, and loading requirements.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Then plan the panels</h2><p>
      Usable width, join seam loss, print direction, and seam orientation
      determine purchase length. The <a href="/calculators/quilt-backing/"
        >quilt backing calculator</a
      > compares valid panel directions; next check the <a
        href="/calculators/quilt-batting/">batting size</a
      >.
    </p>
  </section>
</GuidePage>
